{{ with .Policy }}<p>Version {{ .Version }} · Effective {{ .EffectiveAt.UTC.Format "January 2, 2006" }}</p><div class="policy-text">{{ .TermsText }}</div><h2>Privacy policy</h2><div class="policy-text">{{ .PrivacyText }}</div>{{ else }}<p class="fine">Updated {{ .TermsUpdated }}</p>
<h2>Your passage</h2><p>The expedition runs January 24–February 5, 2028. Fares are per person in USD. Your group selects cabin types and the number of berths; specific cabin numbers and deck locations are not guaranteed. We will try to match M, F or co-ed roommate preferences in shared twin cabins. Triple and quad cabins default to co-ed.</p>
<h2>Payment options</h2><p>Choose full payment at signup or five installments: at booking, January 1, April 1, July 1 and October 1, 2027. Full payment in bitcoin receives a 5% passage discount. Launch purchases are Bitcoin-only. Installments use the standard fare. Merchandise is separate, paid upfront, and collected onboard.</p>
<h2>Operator deposit and payment deadline</h2><p>The operator requires a 20% deposit per traveler as they book and describes that deposit as non-refundable. The operator requires final payment 70 days before departure: November 15, 2027, assuming the January 24 departure date. Our installment plan finishes earlier, on October 1, 2027. Our guest cancellation policy appears below.</p>
<h2>Cabin availability and confirmation</h2><p>Our cabin allocation is currently held on a right-of-first-refusal basis. If another passenger requests a held cabin, the operator can require us to confirm it with a deposit or release it within 24–48 hours. This is an operator hold, not a confirmed passenger booking. Contact inbox@btcpp.dev for assistance with booking confirmation or availability.</p>
<h2>Insurance you must arrange</h2><p>Travel insurance is required and is not included in your fare. It must cover medical treatment, accidents, evacuation and repatriation in Antarctica. The operator currently requires at least EUR/USD 100,000 per person for medical evacuation and repatriation. Ask your insurer to confirm coverage for this destination and your planned activities. Cancellation and interruption cover are strongly recommended; they are separate from the mandatory medical and evacuation cover. We will confirm proof-of-insurance requirements before travel.</p><p><a href="https://oceanwide-expeditions.com/faq/what-type-of-insurance-do-you-recommend-for-the-voyages" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Operator insurance requirements ↗</a></p>
<h2>Published voyage inclusions</h2><p>The operator lists accommodation, onboard meals and snacks, coffee and tea, guided Zodiac outings, lectures, loan boots and snowshoes, embarkation-day luggage transfer, a scheduled disembarkation airport transfer, service taxes and port charges. Offered Basecamp activities are included without an activity surcharge. Final inclusions will be checked against our group confirmation.</p>
<h2>Costs to plan for separately</h2><p>Flights, pre- and post-cruise stays, meals ashore, passports and visas, government arrival/departure taxes, insurance, gratuities and personal purchases are excluded. The cruise does not supply parkas. The bitcoin++ parka is a separate organizer arrangement; contact us about inclusion and delivery. Cruise port charges do not settle the tax treatment of our own booking.</p>
<h2>Activities and itinerary changes</h2><p>Landings, wildlife sightings and individual activities are not guaranteed. Weather, ice, permits and environmental restrictions can change the route and program. The expedition leader decides the final plan. Activities depend on safe conditions, capacity, appropriate equipment and participant suitability. Follow the crew’s safety and environmental instructions. Activity registration and equipment requirements will be confirmed in your departure information.</p>
<h2>Traveler information and documents</h2><p>Each traveler must provide accurate personal information, complete required operator forms and carry the necessary passport, visas and other travel documents. Tell the operator about health or mobility needs relevant to safe participation through its designated process. Oceanwide requires a Personal Information Form (PIF), including personal, passport, emergency-contact and medical information. Its published guidance says to return the PIF within one month of booking. Boot sizing and activity forms are included where applicable. Insurance policy details are also requested after booking. We will provide the operator’s current form or personal completion link and confirm any departure-specific instructions or additional medical clearance requirements. A group purchaser’s booking acceptance does not replace each traveler’s required forms.</p>
<h2>Guest payment, cancellation and substitutions</h2><p><strong>Final guest payment is due by the end of October 1, 2027, in America/Chicago time. Refund eligibility ends at the start of that date.</strong></p><p>Cancellation requests received before 12:00 a.m. on October 1, 2027, in America/Chicago time are eligible for a refund of passage payments received, less the initial 20% deposit, which is non-refundable. No refund is available for guest cancellations received at or after that cutoff. Send cancellation requests to inbox@btcpp.dev. Passenger substitutions are not permitted.</p><h2>Bitcoin refund valuation</h2><p>Bitcoin payments are valued in USD at their value on the day each payment was received. Refund entitlement is calculated from those recorded USD amounts, less the non-refundable deposit. A refund paid in Bitcoin is converted from the refundable USD amount at the exchange rate when the refund is sent; the number of satoshis returned may differ from the number originally paid.</p>
<h2>Our expedition supplier</h2><p>We are booking directly with Oceanwide Expeditions. Our written group agreement and the applicable Oceanwide requirements form the supplier basis for these booking terms. Adventure Life is an itinerary reference only; its booking contract and forms do not apply to our direct booking. Your booking with bitcoin++ is subject to the guest booking terms accepted at checkout.</p>
<h2>Missed installments and abandonment</h2><p>Installments are due by the end of their stated date in Texas time (America/Chicago). We send reminders 14 days before, 4 days before, on the due date, and every other day overdue through day 28. If an installment remains unpaid for 30 days after its deadline, the reservation is marked abandoned, its berths released, and all payments already made forfeited. We notify the purchaser and our expedition team when forfeiture is completed.</p><p>Abandonment for non-payment is distinct from a guest-requested cancellation. An unpaid checkout hold simply expires; it is not a confirmed booking and does not trigger forfeiture. Payment processing or reconciliation issues require review before abandonment. Your accepted booking terms are retained with your purchase.</p>
<h2>Operator references and questions</h2><p>Source review: October 23, 2026. <a href="https://oceanwide-expeditions.com/antarctica/cruises/otl28-28-basecamp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">departure-specific voyage information</a> and <a href="https://oceanwide-expeditions.com/page/terms-and-conditions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">operator terms</a>. These links are reference material, not automatic acceptance of another business’s contract.</p><p>For booking questions, cancellation requests or assistance with traveler requirements, contact <a href="mailto:inbox@btcpp.dev">inbox@btcpp.dev</a>. The versioned terms and privacy policy accepted at checkout are retained with your purchase.</p>{{ end }}
